\f2\i \cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Shit. They\'92re assigning me the game of Pick the Terrorists
\f1\i0 . Alexander knew the drill: he\'92d be the photogenic face announcing whatever narrative the hollow men in windowless rooms had already scripted. Some poor sods would be dragged before cameras, and Alexander would be required to theatrically declare them the perpetrators while unseen hands pulled the strings. He eyed off the cop with the sniper rifle, wondering if today\'92s scapegoats were already marked for \'93resisting arrest.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93So. How about it?\'94 a cop persisted.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93How about what?\'94 Alexander was becoming antagonistic.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Are the executions real?\'94\
